{
 "_lane": "Shiva (FFX aeon; the ice queen; the possessed Shiva of Chapter III link 5 and a summon in ten more chapters): the idle's gown is the costume; cast and hurt are the same gown bent (painted keys), attack, KO and Overdrive are other drawings (ribbons and a crown, a figure lying flat, a floating figure in white), so those three are AUTHORED. Cut by polygons and the underlaps (no SAM): the dreadlock hair with its ice spears, the far leg, the gown's skirt and train, the far arm, the body (torso and neck base), the near leg, the raised arm and the head. The attack key is posed by hand from the cast key (a forward lean and an arm swing, marks at the idle's head and feet): every fit of it against the ribbon-and-crown drawing failed the planted-feet check (feet 0.034 to 0.040 off). Game case: FFX only (an FFX aeon's painting set); the rig stays OFF. EXPRESSIVE KEYS (rig-expressive-2 lane, 2026-10-19): the hurt and attack keys show EVERY part as pieces cut from that pose's own painting (the attack painting is another drawing: ribbons, ice crown, braid). The pieces are masks (tools/rig/subjects/shiva-x.masks: the painting's pixels partitioned among the parts by the baseline hurt key's silhouettes (autopart.py) or by hand-drawn seeds (seeds-attack.json, autoseed.py), dilated 16 px for the underlap); the hurt and attack keys' bone transforms are placed by jfit.py so every joint the hole test watches sits inside its own pieces. The attack key hides legB and armD (the painting has one visible leg and its glove belongs to the hair piece); the idle, cast, KO and Overdrive keys are the shipped rig's.",
